      "content": "While aggressive stacking is tempting, medical guidelines and safety data do not support maximizing dosage to \"push\" fat burning, as excessive doses of green tea extract and theobromine can cause severe heart palpitations, seizures, and liver damage. Reaching a truly effective therapeutic window for weight loss risks becomes significantly dangerous far above standard supplement levels, which are generally limited to a combined 300–400mg of caffeine daily for most adults. Instead of higher doses, prioritize consistent intense exercise and a slight calorie deficit, which provide far more sustained and safe fat loss benefits than any possible supplement stack.",
